Mutex vs Condition Variable
Mutex	                              Condition Variable
Provides mutual exclusion	|        Allows threads to wait for a condition
Uses lock() and unlock()	|           Uses wait() and notify_one()
Prevents simultaneous access|        	Avoids busy waiting
Does not itself provide notification	|     Works together with a mutex

Important interview points:
1. A condition variable always works with a mutex in C++.
2. wait() releases the mutex while sleeping.
3. After notification, the waiting thread reacquires the mutex.
4. Always check the condition using a predicate because spurious wakeups are possible.
5. notify_one() wakes one waiting thread; notify_all() wakes all waiting threads.
Remember the difference:
- Mutex: Only one thread can access the critical section at a time.
- Condition Variable: A thread can sleep until a particular condition becomes true.
